---
import LegalLayout from '../components/ui/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site.ts';
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  path="/terms/"
  description="The terms on which we provide this website and, separately, our services."
  updated="August 2026"
>
  <h2>These terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms govern your use of this website. They are not the terms of any engagement between
    us — project work is governed by a separate written agreement signed by both parties, and that
    agreement takes precedence over anything on this page.
  </p>

  <h2>Using this website</h2>
  <p>You may browse, read and share this website freely. You may not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Use it in a way that damages it, or interferes with anyone else's use of it.</li>
    <li>Attempt to gain unauthorised access to any part of it or to any connected system.</li>
    <li>Copy substantial portions of its content and present them as your own.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Content on this site</h2>
  <p>
    The text, design, code and graphics on this website belong to {site.legalName} unless stated
    otherwise. You may quote short passages with attribution and a link.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    We keep this site accurate and current, but it is provided for general information. Timelines,
    price ranges and capabilities described here are indicative. Nothing on this website is an offer
    capable of acceptance, and nothing here forms a contract.
  </p>

  <h2>Your project work</h2>
  <p>
    Any development, consultancy or subscription service we provide is governed by a written
    agreement covering scope, fees, timelines, intellectual property, confidentiality and support.
    Where this website and that agreement differ, the agreement applies.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    This site links to services we do not control. We are not responsible for their content,
    availability or practices.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for loss arising from your use of this
    website. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot lawfully be limited.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the United Arab Emirates, and the courts of the UAE have
    exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute arising from them.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
